{#- RECUPERACIÓN ACTIVA — the recovery-day sibling of /members/movilidad/.
    Home doc: `recovery-brief.md`. Built September 4, 2026 from section B of
    Iván's "Sistema Maestro de Movilidad" source doc (Día Cualquiera).

    Two questions -> one of 15 routines (sport x duration). Same engine, same
    setup pattern and the same CSS file as /members/movilidad/ and
    /members/activacion/. Fourth tool on the activation engine.

    *** THE SIX DECISIONS TAKEN BEFORE BUILDING, all Iván's. Read these first:

    1. THE 30-MINUTE CORES WERE REBALANCED. Section B's cores were two-thirds
       exercises the library already had — six of nine in every sport, spread
       across /members/core/ and /members/activacion/. Section A worked because
       posterior chain, anterior hip and shoulder decompression are different
       jobs; section B converged on general mobility flow, which the activation
       matrix already does in twelve minutes.
       *** SO THE CORES NOW LEAD WITH WHAT ONLY THIS TOOL CAN DO: slow CARs,
       flows, long passive holds, PNF and balance — the things that do not fit
       in the twelve minutes before a ride. The shared movements are connective
       tissue, not the opening. A verification check measures the overlap
       against the activation matrix so the rebalance stays provable. ***

    2. NO SHOULDER DISLOCATES. Third attempt: the source has them in the
       cyclist, swimmer AND triathlete routines. `activation-matrix.md` says in
       bold "Do not restore dislocates" — competitive swimmers are typically LAX
       at the anterior capsule, not stiff, and end-range external rotation plus
       extension on a long lever is the same class of error as the sleeper
       stretch. One shared library means the cyclist version cannot be uncapped
       either. What ships is `wallAngel` (mat and wall) with a CAPPED stick
       pass-through as its variant, whose cue carries the cap.

    3. MAT AND WALL BASE, everything else as `variants` — identical to
       /members/movilidad/, and now also a consistency argument: an athlete who
       learned the "Cambiar ejercicio" button on that tool looks for it here.
       Two casualties from the source: the kettlebell HALO (no mat-only
       equivalent, and its goal is already covered) and the STEP for eccentric
       calf raises, which became floor eccentrics with the step as a variant.

    4. THE STRENGTH AND ACTIVATION CONTENT STAYS, AND THE BLOCKS SAY SO.
       Roughly a third of section B is clamshells, bird-dogs, side planks,
       banded walks, dead bugs, bear crawls, scapular push-ups and Y-T-W-L —
       that is activation and strength work, not mobility. It is what makes a
       recovery day worth doing, so it stays, but the phase is NAMED
       "Activación" rather than hidden inside a mobility routine.
       *** AND THE COPY SAYS THIS IS A SESSION, NOT A REST DAY. methodology.md
       §7 has real placement rules; thirty minutes with fifteen of glute and
       core work is an easy session. Do not let the copy imply it is free. ***

    5. NO JEFFERSON CURLS. Unloaded helps, but it is segmental spinal flexion
       under a long lever, unsupervised, for a population with a lot of
       low-back history — the highest-risk item in section B after dislocates.
       Replaced by `rollDown`, a supine segmental roll-down: same job,
       bodyweight, lying down, and consistent with the roll-ups the source
       already had in the general routine.

    6. IT IS CALLED RECUPERACIÓN ACTIVA, which is what the source doc calls it.
       Not "movilidad" — see decision 4.

    Two things the source got RIGHT that must not be "fixed" later:
      - FROG POSE belongs here, on a recovery day, on fresh tissue. It was cut
        from /members/movilidad/ for exactly that reason. The two tools
        differing on this is correct, not an inconsistency.
      - The 60-minute tiers here are real content — sun salutations, Yin,
        thoracic CARs — not the savasana padding section A's 60 tier had.

    Also trimmed: single-leg balance with eyes closed was 2 minutes in the
    source. People fall. 40s per side.

    *** EVERY NOTE ABOUT THIS PAGE BELONGS IN THIS BLOCK. Almost the whole page
    is inside {% raw %}, where a Nunjucks comment is NOT a comment — it is
    literal text that renders to the reader. That happened on the activation
    page on Sept 3, 2026 and Iván saw it live. `automation/build-sanity.js` now
    fails the build on any surviving template delimiter; the simpler rule is to
    write the note here or use an HTML comment. -#}
